    "body": "### Problem\n\nUpdated to nightly both nvim and wezterm, same problem. Did not happen with 0.12. I recently upgraded to 0.13 and it started happening immediately. Possibly a plugin screwing something up but no new plugins. When I resize the window borders the problem goes away. It seems that neovim is getting the wrong terminal width or height, possibly off by 1 (rounding or something). Usually it is not as bad as in the image. Usually it is just a little off at the bottom. \n\n<img width=\"2412\" height=\"1047\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d1932c4-eee4-46d2-83d7-8f66a91a3273\" />\n\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAll I can say is that there were no issues before updating to 0.13 with no changes to wezterm. It does not seem to happen in a windows terminal. I don't know about neovide because it is now crashing with invalid parameter when I try to use it.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nLayout to be correct. The image says it all. Again, if I rescale the border of wezterm it works fine. It worked fine before updating to 0.13. It might be some issue with wezterm itself or some strange confluence of things on my system but it did not happen prior to 0.13 suggesting that it is something related to specifically 0.13.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1915+gc5641b2bfb\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nBest I can tell, no\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWin11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwzterm/nightly\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nnot used\n\n### Installation\n\nrepo",
